    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0501" n="406" xml:id="pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8410: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-04T15:00:00+08:00">December 4, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 4—1:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>588. Embassy’s 583, December 3, 3 p.m. Following telegram has been received from
                    Tsingtau: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 4, 10 a.m. Situation remains quiet. Chinese who were arrested
                            have been released. Chinese authorities regard Japanese action as
                            designed to force out present Mayor and his administration.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Nanking informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
